MariaDB/MySQL user defined functions (UDFs) that talk to memcached
servers through libmemcached. They let SQL statements and triggers
get, set, delete, increment and manage keys on memcached.

This is the echoCTF fork, which fixes memory corruption and leaks,
adds memc_mset(), memc_server_list(), memc_server_remove() and returns
NULL on NULL keys.

Load the functions with:
  mysql < /usr/local/share/memcached_functions_mysql/install_functions.sql
